sanctioned: this program round-trips nullable fields through a codec-backed Ipe.Db.Store on sqlite::memory:. Ipe.Db.Store is an Ipê-only addition with no counterpart in the reference backend, and Ipê emits Rust+sqlx while the reference emits a different backend, so a shared Main.ipe cannot run on both. Ipê's output is recorded as the correct reference. The output lines assert, in order: (1) a row written with a `Maybe String`, `Maybe Int`, `Maybe Float`, and `Maybe Bool` all `Nothing` reads back `Nothing` for each through `get` (SQL NULL is never decoded as `Just ""`, nor as a decode error); (2) `Just ""`, `Just 0`, `Just 3.0`, `Just False` read back unchanged (the empty string and zero are values, not NULL); (3) `Just "NULL"` reads back unchanged (the text "NULL" is not an in-band NULL marker) and a REAL outside the positional range decodes exactly; (4) `all` decodes every row with the same distinction; (5) `findBy` and (6) `findWhere` on the NULL row read `Nothing`; (7) an ascending query on the nullable int orders the NULL row first and (8) a descending one last; (9) a codec whose field is a plain `String` refuses the NULL row with a typed error.
